00:57:30,200 --> 00:57:31,711
That was Ethereum, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

896
00:57:31,720 --> 00:57:34,830
Did you guys qualify for that bug bounty or?

897
00:57:34,840 --> 00:57:38,990
No, we we since we were a vendor for them, we didn't we didn't qualify for.

898
00:57:38,990 --> 00:57:42,030
I I wish I wish it would have been it would have been a lot of money.

899
00:57:42,040 --> 00:57:44,550
No, we in the early days of the company,

900
00:57:44,560 --> 00:57:51,630
we actually thought about using bug bounties as the primary source of revenue, right?

901
00:57:51,630 --> 00:57:53,190
Cuz like some of them get pretty high.

902
00:57:53,200 --> 00:57:59,350
And this thing is actually quite good at finding security bugs, too, that that human beings sometimes miss.

903
00:57:59,360 --> 00:58:03,190
And so, that was certainly a thing we thought about.

904
00:58:03,190 --> 00:58:06,390
In the end, we thought that that was a little bit adversarial.

905
00:58:06,400 --> 00:58:10,670
And that we would rather be embedded with our customer's engineering team.

906
00:58:10,670 --> 00:58:15,830
and like making them successful and like improving their lives.

907
00:58:15,830 --> 00:58:17,590
making it easier for them to do their job.

908
00:58:17,590 --> 00:58:19,230
We thought that in the long term,

909
00:58:19,230 --> 00:58:24,230
that would lead to better customer relationships than this like come in from the outside.

910
00:58:24,230 --> 00:58:25,910
and claim bounties model.

911
00:58:25,920 --> 00:58:28,870
But I I assume somebody's going to be using.

912
00:58:28,880 --> 00:58:32,870
either DST or AI or something else to claim bug bounties very soon.

913
00:58:32,880 --> 00:58:35,310
Mhm, fair enough.

914
00:58:35,310 --> 00:58:38,630
No, no, I I'd say it's a exciting kind of future out there.

915
00:58:38,630 --> 00:58:40,550
As we wrap up in closing thoughts,

916
00:58:40,550 --> 00:58:44,670
what advice would you give to our listeners about improving their own testing practices.

917
00:58:44,670 --> 00:58:48,070
or evolving their, you know, platforms to get ready for DST?

918
00:58:48,080 --> 00:58:50,790
Right.

919
00:58:50,790 --> 00:58:54,471
It's really The thing I said towards the start of this is I think the single most important. piece of advice.

920
00:58:54,480 --> 00:59:01,230
Anytime you see a bug in production, any single time, it is two bugs.

921
00:59:01,240 --> 00:59:02,750
It is two bugs.

922
00:59:02,750 --> 00:59:04,990
It is a bug in your code, but it's also a bug in your tests.

923
00:59:05,000 --> 00:59:09,750
And you should demand more from your tests.

924
00:59:09,750 --> 00:59:13,990
You should cultivate the attitude that it is unacceptable for things to go wrong in production.

925
00:59:14,000 --> 00:59:16,710
And that if a thing does go wrong in production,

926
00:59:16,710 --> 00:59:19,830
you should be asking yourself, what could we have done differently.

927
00:59:19,840 --> 00:59:22,350
that would mean that we found this ahead of time?

928
00:59:22,360 --> 00:59:24,150
Awesome.

929
00:59:24,150 --> 00:59:27,110
For all those who want to learn more, how How they do so and where?

930
00:59:27,120 --> 00:59:28,670
Oh, yeah.

931
00:59:28,670 --> 00:59:30,510
There's a lot of people who've written good stuff about this.

932
00:59:30,510 --> 00:59:34,150
We have some material on our website antithesis.com.

933
00:59:34,150 --> 00:59:40,110
The other people who have talked the loudest and the most about DST, the FoundationDB team, has written a bunch of stuff about this.

934
00:59:40,120 --> 00:59:44,550
They're now at Apple and and a lot of them are at Snowflake, but they've written a ton of good stuff.

935
00:59:44,550 --> 00:59:51,310
The FoundationDB paper that came out a few years ago and was in SIGMOD is very good.

936
00:59:51,310 --> 00:59:54,030
I can send you a link to that. It's got a whole section on how we did DST.

937
00:59:54,040 --> 00:59:57,710
The people at TigerBeetle have written some really good stuff about this.

938
00:59:57,720 --> 01:00:00,030
They've done a very good job at it.

939
